{"id":"da11df7496b5d39e2163b13b1495c727c21a589b","axis":"silent","repo":"envoyproxy/envoy","sha":"da11df7496b5d39e2163b13b1495c727c21a589b","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"api/envoy/extensions/bootstrap/dynamic_modules/v3/dynamic_modules.proto","lines":["@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ option (udpa.annotations.file_status).package_version_status = ACTIVE;"," // Bootstrap extensions run on the main thread and are initialized when Envoy starts. They can:"," //"," // * Perform initialization tasks when the server is initialized.","-// * Perform per-worker thread initialization when worker threads start.","+// * Run code on every worker thread."," // * Access server-level resources like the cluster manager and dispatcher."," //"," message DynamicModuleBootstrapExtension {"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"changelogs/current/new_features/dynamic_modules__bootstrap-cluster-writer.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@","+Added a cluster writer to the dynamic module bootstrap extension. Once a module calls","+``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_enable_cluster_writer``, it can add, update and","+remove clusters, and it learns when each write becomes active. See","+:ref:`Cluster Writer <config_bootstrap_extensions_dynamic_modules_cluster_writer>`."],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"changelogs/current/new_features/dynamic_modules__bootstrap-run-on-all-workers.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@","+Added ``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_run_on_all_workers`` to the dynamic module","+bootstrap extension. It runs a module hook on every worker thread and then a done hook on the main","+thread. See :ref:`Running Code on Workers","+<config_bootstrap_extensions_dynamic_modules_run_on_all_workers>`. The documentation of","+``envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_worker_thread_initialized`` now says that it runs once","+on the main thread, so per-worker setup belongs in this new callback."],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/root/configuration/other_features/bootstrap_extensions/dynamic_modules.rst","lines":["@@ -9,7 +9,8 @@ The Dynamic Modules bootstrap extension allows you to write bootstrap extensions"," This can be used to implement:"," "," * Server initialization logic when Envoy starts.","-* Per-worker-thread initialization logic when worker threads start.","+* Code that runs on every worker thread.","+* Clusters that the module adds, updates and removes."," * Singleton patterns for configuration loading from external services."," * Global state management across filters."," * Background tasks that run on the main thread.","@@ -38,7 +39,8 @@ Lifecycle Hooks"," Bootstrap extensions have two lifecycle hooks:"," "," **onServerInitialized**","-  Called when the server is fully initialized, on the main thread. This is where you can:","+  Called on the main thread once Envoy created its cluster manager and listener manager, and before","+  it starts its workers. Clusters can still be initializing. This is where you can:"," ","   * Load configuration from external services.","   * Initialize global state.","@@ -46,11 +48,80 @@ Bootstrap extensions have two lifecycle hooks:","   * Start background tasks."," "," **onWorkerThreadInitialized**","-  Called once per worker thread when it starts. This is where you can:","-","-  * Initialize per-worker-thread state.","-  * Set up thread-local storage.","-  * Prepare resources for use by filters on this thread.","+  Called once on the main thread after Envoy creates its workers and before it starts their","+  threads. To run code on every worker thread once the server is initialized, see :ref:`Running Code","+  on Workers <config_bootstrap_extensions_dynamic_modules_run_on_all_workers>`.","+","+.. _config_bootstrap_extensions_dynamic_modules_run_on_all_workers:","+","+Running Code on Workers","+-----------------------","+","+A module calls ``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_run_on_all_workers`` on the","+main thread to run its ``envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_worker_event`` hook on every","+worker thread. Once every worker ran the event,","+``envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_run_on_all_workers_done`` runs on the main thread. A","+worker runs the event after it applied the cluster and host changes that Envoy posted to it","+before the call, so the done hook tells the module that every worker can use them. Host health,","+weight and metadata changes that a cluster merges over its :ref:`update_merge_window","+<envoy_v3_api_field_config.cluster.v3.Cluster.CommonLbConfig.update_merge_window>` can reach the","+workers later.","+","+The workers start only after Envoy finishes initializing, so a module must not wait for the done","+hook before it calls ``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_config_signal_init_complete``.","+That call can start the workers and wait until they ran the events posted before it, so a module","+must not hold a lock across it that its worker event hook takes.","+","+.. _config_bootstrap_extensions_dynamic_modules_cluster_writer:","+","+Cluster Writer","+--------------","+","+Once the module calls ``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_enable_cluster_writer``,","+it can add, update and remove clusters. It passes a serialized","+:ref:`Cluster <envoy_v3_api_msg_config.cluster.v3.Cluster>` to","+``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_cluster_writer_add_or_update``, and Envoy","+reports the outcome of each write through","+``envoy_dynamic_module_on_bootstrap_extension_cluster_writer_update_done``. A write is active once","+the cluster finished warming. CDS does not remove the clusters that the module writes, and the","+module should only write clusters that no other component writes. Envoy does not wait for written","+clusters before it finishes initializing, so to serve them from the first request, call","+``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_config_signal_init_complete`` only after their","+writes completed as active.","+","+A written cluster has the same authority as a cluster delivered by CDS, so build clusters from a","+schema that the module owns. On the ADS stream and the xDS-TP authority streams, a written cluster","+holds back the CDS requests while it warms, as a cluster delivered by CDS does, unless its","+:ref:`wait_for_warm_on_init <envoy_v3_api_field_config.cluster.v3.Cluster.wait_for_warm_on_init>`","+is false. While Envoy applies a burst of writes, it holds back the EDS, LEDS and SDS requests on","+those streams, including their ACKs, for about one second, as it does while it applies a CDS","+update. A write that changes a cluster","+rebuilds it and drains its connection pools, so change endpoints through a dynamic module cluster","+instead.","+","+The config dump lists written clusters as dynamic clusters with the ``version_info`` of their last","+change. Envoy does not time out a write that never finishes warming. Such a write holds back the","+CDS requests until the module writes the cluster again or removes it, and a module that holds back","+``envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_config_signal_init_complete`` until its writes","+are active should bound that wait itself.","+","+The cluster writer emits the following statistics with the ``dynamic_modules.cluster_writer.``","+prefix, tagged with ``config_name`` set to the extension name, or ``default`` if it is empty.","+","+.. csv-table::","+  :header: Name, Type, Description","+  :widths: 1, 1, 2","+","+  update_submitted, Counter, Writes that Envoy accepted","+  update_rejected, Counter, Writes that Envoy refused before the server was initialized or after shutdown began","+  update_active, Counter, Writes that became active","+  update_superseded, Counter, Writes that a later write replaced before they became active","+  update_removed, Counter, Writes that a removal ended before they became active","+  update_failed, Counter, Writes that failed when Envoy applied them","+  update_ownership_lost, Counter, Writes that ended because another component removed the cluster","+  ownership_lost, Counter, Clusters that another component replaced or removed","+  clusters_owned, Gauge, Clusters that the module owns","+  updates_pending, Gauge, Writes that are queued or warming"," "," Use Cases"," ---------"],"additions":78,"deletions":7,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/bootstrap/dynamic_modules/BUILD","lines":["@@ -9,19 +9,56 @@ licenses([\"notice\"])  # Apache 2"," "," envoy_extension_package()"," ","+envoy_cc_library(","+    name = \"cluster_writer_lib\",","+    srcs = [\"cluster_writer.cc\"],","+    hdrs = [\"cluster_writer.h\"],","+    deps = [","+        \"//envoy/common:exception_lib\",","+        \"//envoy/common:time_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/config:grpc_mux_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/config:xds_manager_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/event:schedulable_cb_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/init:manager_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/server:factory_context_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/singleton:manager_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/stats:stats_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/upstream:cluster_manager_interface\",","+        \"//source/common/common:fmt_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/common:logger_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/config:dependent_type_urls_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/config:resource_name_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/init:target_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/protobuf:utility_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/stats:utility_lib\",","+        \"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules:dynamic_modules_lib\",","+        \"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules/abi\",","+        \"@abseil-cpp//absl/container:flat_hash_set\",","+        \"@abseil-cpp//absl/container:node_hash_map\",","+        \"@abseil-cpp//absl/status\",","+        \"@abseil-cpp//absl/strings\",","+        \"@envoy_api//envoy/config/cluster/v3:pkg_cc_proto\",","+    ],","+)","+"," envoy_cc_library(","     name = \"extension_config_lib\",","     srcs = [\"extension_config.cc\"],","     hdrs = [\"extension_config.h\"],","     deps = [","+        \":cluster_writer_lib\",","+        \"//envoy/common:optref_lib\",","         \"//envoy/event:dispatcher_interface\",","         \"//envoy/http:async_client_interface\",","         \"//envoy/server:factory_context_interface\",","         \"//envoy/server:listener_manager_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/server:options_interface\",","         \"//envoy/stats:stats_interface\",","+        \"//envoy/thread_local:thread_local_interface\",","         \"//source/common/buffer:buffer_lib\",","         \"//source/common/common:assert_lib\",","         \"//source/common/common:logger_lib\",","+        \"//source/common/common:thread_lib\",","         \"//source/common/http:message_lib\",","         \"//source/common/init:target_lib\",","         \"//source/common/stats:utility_lib\",","@@ -57,6 +94,7 @@ envoy_cc_library(","         \"//source/common/stats:symbol_table_lib\",","         \"//source/common/stats:utility_lib\",","         \"//source/extensions/dynamic_modules:dynamic_modules_lib\",","+        \"@abseil-cpp//absl/strings\",","     ],"," )"," "],"additions":38,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/bootstrap/dynamic_modules/abi_impl.cc","lines":["@@ -14,10 +14,13 @@"," #include \"source/extensions/bootstrap/dynamic_modules/extension_config.h\""," #include \"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/abi/abi.h\""," ","+#include \"absl/strings/str_cat.h\"","+"," using Envoy::Extensions::Bootstrap::DynamicModules::DynamicModuleBootstrapExtension;"," using Envoy::Extensions::Bootstrap::DynamicModules::DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig;"," using Envoy::Extensions::Bootstrap::DynamicModules::DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfigScheduler;"," using Envoy::Extensions::Bootstrap::DynamicModules::DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionTimer;","+using Envoy::Extensions::Bootstrap::DynamicModules::DynamicModuleClusterWriter;"," using Envoy::Extensions::DynamicModules::MetricRegistry;"," "," namespace {","@@ -67,6 +70,12 @@ void envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_config_scheduler_commit("," void envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_config_signal_init_complete(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr) {","   auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    // Envoy cannot finish initializing without the signal, so deliver it on the main thread.","+    config->postSignalInitComplete();","+    return;","+  }","   config->signalInitComplete();"," }"," ","@@ -78,6 +87,10 @@ envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_http_callout(","     uint64_t* callout_id_out, envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer cluster_name,","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_http_header* headers, size_t headers_size,","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer body, uint64_t timeout_milliseconds) {","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return envoy_dynamic_module_type_http_callout_init_result_CannotCreateRequest;","+  }","   auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);"," ","   // Build the HTTP request message.","@@ -514,6 +527,10 @@ envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_timer_new("," ","   // Allocate the timer wrapper first so we can capture a stable heap pointer in the callback.","   auto* timer_wrapper = new DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionTimer(config->weak_from_this());","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return static_cast<void*>(timer_wrapper);","+  }"," ","   // Create the timer on the main thread dispatcher. The callback captures a weak_ptr to the config","   // to safely handle the case where the config is destroyed before the timer fires. The","@@ -538,20 +555,39 @@ envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_timer_new("," void envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_timer_enable(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_timer_module_ptr timer_ptr,","     uint64_t delay_milliseconds) {","-  auto* timer = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionTimer*>(timer_ptr);","-  timer->timer().enableTimer(std::chrono::milliseconds(delay_milliseconds));","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return;","+  }","+  Envoy::OptRef<Envoy::Event::Timer> timer =","+      static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionTimer*>(timer_ptr)->timer();","+  if (timer.has_value()) {","+    timer->enableTimer(std::chrono::milliseconds(delay_milliseconds));","+  }"," }"," "," void envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_timer_disable(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_timer_module_ptr timer_ptr) {","-  auto* timer = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionTimer*>(timer_ptr);","-  timer->timer().disableTimer();","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return;","+  }","+  Envoy::OptRef<Envoy::Event::Timer> timer =","+      static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionTimer*>(timer_ptr)->timer();","+  if (timer.has_value()) {","+    timer->disableTimer();","+  }"," }"," "," bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_timer_enabled(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_timer_module_ptr timer_ptr) {","-  auto* timer = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionTimer*>(timer_ptr);","-  return timer->timer().enabled();","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return false;","+  }","+  Envoy::OptRef<Envoy::Event::Timer> timer =","+      static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionTimer*>(timer_ptr)->timer();","+  return timer.has_value() && timer->enabled();"," }"," "," void envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_timer_delete(","@@ -574,6 +610,10 @@ void envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_timer_delete("," bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_file_watcher_add_watch(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr,","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer path, uint32_t events) {","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return false;","+  }","   auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);"," ","   // Create a new filesystem watcher for this path. Envoy owns the watcher lifetime.","@@ -603,6 +643,10 @@ bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_file_watcher_add_watch("," void envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_admin_set_response(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr,","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer response_body) {","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return;","+  }","   auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);","   if (response_body.ptr != nullptr && response_body.length > 0) {","     config->admin_response_body_.assign(response_body.ptr, response_body.length);","@@ -613,8 +657,12 @@ bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_register_admin_handler(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr,","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer path_prefix,","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer help_text, bool removable, bool mutates_server_state) {","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return false;","+  }","   auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);","-  Envoy::OptRef<Envoy::Server::Admin> admin = config->context_.admin();","+  Envoy::OptRef<Envoy::Server::Admin> admin = config->admin();","   if (!admin.has_value()) {","     return false;","   }","@@ -622,14 +670,17 @@ bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_register_admin_handler(","   const std::string prefix_str(path_prefix.ptr, path_prefix.length);","   const std::string help_str(help_text.ptr, help_text.length);"," ","-  // Capture a shared_ptr to the config to ensure it stays alive during admin handler callbacks.","-  auto config_shared = config->shared_from_this();","-","+  // The admin server outlives the bootstrap extensions, so the handler must not keep the config","+  // alive.","   return admin->addHandler(","       prefix_str, help_str,","-      [config_shared](Envoy::Http::ResponseHeaderMap& response_headers,","-                      Envoy::Buffer::Instance& response,","-                      Envoy::Server::AdminStream& admin_stream) -> Envoy::Http::Code {","+      [weak_config = config->weak_from_this()](","+          Envoy::Http::ResponseHeaderMap& response_headers, Envoy::Buffer::Instance& response,","+          Envoy::Server::AdminStream& admin_stream) -> Envoy::Http::Code {","+        std::shared_ptr<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig> config_shared = weak_config.lock();","+        if (config_shared == nullptr) {","+          return Envoy::Http::Code::NotFound;","+        }","         const auto& request_headers = admin_stream.getRequestHeaders();","         const auto method_entry = request_headers.getMethodValue();","         const auto path_entry = request_headers.getPathValue();","@@ -669,8 +720,12 @@ bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_register_admin_handler("," bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_remove_admin_handler(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr,","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer path_prefix) {","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return false;","+  }","   auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);","-  Envoy::OptRef<Envoy::Server::Admin> admin = config->context_.admin();","+  Envoy::OptRef<Envoy::Server::Admin> admin = config->admin();","   if (!admin.has_value()) {","     return false;","   }","@@ -683,6 +738,10 @@ bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_remove_admin_handler("," "," bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_enable_cluster_lifecycle(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr) {","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return false;","+  }","   auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);","   return config->enableClusterLifecycle();"," }","@@ -691,8 +750,74 @@ bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_enable_cluster_lifecycle("," "," bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_enable_listener_lifecycle(","     envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr) {","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return false;","+  }","   auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);","   return config->enableListenerLifecycle();"," }"," ","+// -------------------- Run On All Workers Callbacks --------------------","+","+bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_run_on_all_workers(","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr,","+    uint64_t event_id) {","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return false;","+  }","+  auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);","+  return config->runOnAllWorkers(event_id);","+}","+","+// -------------------- Cluster Writer Callbacks --------------------","+","+bool envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_enable_cluster_writer(","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr) {","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return false;","+  }","+  auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);","+  return config->enableClusterWriter();","+}","+","+envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_cluster_writer_update_result","+envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_cluster_writer_add_or_update(","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr,","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer cluster_name,","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer cluster,","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer version_info, uint64_t* update_id_out) {","+  *update_id_out = 0;","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_cluster_writer_update_result_NotAllowed;","+  }","+  auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);","+  DynamicModuleClusterWriter* cluster_writer = config->cluster_writer_.get();","+  if (cluster_writer == nullptr) {","+    return envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_cluster_writer_update_result_NotAllowed;","+  }","+  return cluster_writer->addOrUpdateCluster(","+      {cluster_name.ptr, cluster_name.length}, {cluster.ptr, cluster.length},","+      {version_info.ptr, version_info.length}, *update_id_out);","+}","+","+envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_cluster_writer_removal_result","+envoy_dynamic_module_callback_bootstrap_extension_cluster_writer_remove(","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_extension_config_envoy_ptr extension_config_envoy_ptr,","+    envoy_dynamic_module_type_module_buffer cluster_name) {","+  if (!Envoy::Thread::MainThread::isMainOrTestThread()) {","+    IS_ENVOY_BUG(absl::StrCat(__func__, \" must be called on the main thread\"));","+    return envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_cluster_writer_removal_result_NotAllowed;","+  }","+  auto* config = static_cast<DynamicModuleBootstrapExtensionConfig*>(extension_config_envoy_ptr);","+  DynamicModuleClusterWriter* cluster_writer = config->cluster_writer_.get();","+  if (cluster_writer == nullptr) {","+    return envoy_dynamic_module_type_bootstrap_cluster_writer_removal_result_NotAllowed;","+  }","+  return cluster_writer->removeCluster({cluster_name.ptr, cluster_name.length});","+}","+"," } // extern \"C\""],"additions":139,"deletions":14,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/bootstrap/dynamic_modules/cluster_writer.cc","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,517 @@","+#include \"source/extensions/bootstrap/dynamic_modules/cluster_writer.h\"","+","+#include <algorithm>","+#include <chrono>","+#include <memory>","+#include <utility>","+","+#include \"envoy/common/exception.h\"","+#include \"envoy/common/time.h\"","+#include \"envoy/config/cluster/v3/cluster.pb.h\"","+#include \"envoy/config/cluster/v3/cluster.pb.validate.h\"","+#include \"envoy/config/grpc_mux.h\"","+#include \"envoy/config/xds_manager.h\"","+#include \"envoy/init/manager.h\"","+#include \"envoy/singleton/manager.h\"","+","+#include \"source/common/common/fmt.h\"","+#include \"source/common/config/dependent_type_urls.h\"","+#include \"source/common/config/resource_name.h\"","+#include \"source/common/protobuf/utility.h\"","+#include \"source/common/stats/utility.h\"","+#include \"source/extensions/dynamic_modules/dynamic_module_stats.h\"","+","+#include \"absl/container/flat_hash_set.h\"","+#include \"absl/strings/str_cat.h\"","+","+namespace Envoy {","+namespace Extensions {","+namespace Bootstrap {","+namespace DynamicModules {","+","+namespace {","+","+// How long an apply pass may run before it yields to the event loop.","+constexpr std::chrono::milliseconds ApplyPassBudget{5};","+// How long the passes of a burst may hold back the requests of the dependent xDS types.","+constexpr std::chrono::milliseconds MaxDependentTypePause{1000};","+constexpr absl::string_view ClusterWriterStatPrefix = \"cluster_writer\";","+","+} // namespace","+","+// The state that the cluster writers of a server share. Their apply passes hold back the requests","+// of the xDS types that clusters depend on with one pause, so that its time limit holds when their","+// bursts overlap.","+class ClusterWriterSharedState : public Singleton::Instance {","+public:","+  static std::shared_ptr<ClusterWriterSharedState>","+  get(Server::Configuration::ServerFactoryContext& context);","+","+  // The writers whose burst of writes is not fully applied yet.","+  absl::flat_hash_set<const DynamicModuleClusterWriter*> writers_applying_;","+  Config::ScopedResume dependent_type_pause_;","+  MonotonicTime dependent_type_pause_start